WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:18.870 --> 01:19.871
Oh dear.

01:21.498 --> 01:23.374
Poems aren't that hard.

01:24.209 --> 01:26.795
Just write down what you'd like to say.

01:26.878 --> 01:28.129
That's a poem.

01:30.507 --> 01:32.300
Ok-sim, make some food.

01:32.383 --> 01:34.594
Look here, I want some food.

01:35.136 --> 01:37.806
Mom, give me food. Food. Food.

01:38.306 --> 01:40.433
Stop asking me for food.

01:40.975 --> 01:43.978
Ok-sim's life has flown by,
just feeding her family.

01:45.230 --> 01:48.650
The words you've held
deep in your heart all your life.

01:49.818 --> 01:53.029
"Loyalty and Filial Piety"
by Lee Byeong-seon.

01:54.114 --> 01:56.991
Eyes are fading, ears are fading.

01:57.784 --> 02:02.580
Listen, my son and daughter,
my back is killing me.

02:03.081 --> 02:05.792
Come see me more and more.

02:07.836 --> 02:10.839
Someone hasn't been able to write
a single letter.

02:12.006 --> 02:14.968
Just write down
what you want to say the most.

02:16.010 --> 02:17.929
That'll be the best poem of your life.

02:38.825 --> 02:40.201
I had no idea back then

02:41.369 --> 02:43.454
that I would ever turn 70.

02:59.846 --> 03:01.264
I had no idea back then…

03:03.600 --> 03:05.685
that what I'd want to say the most at 70

03:06.769 --> 03:09.564
would be the word
I used to say all the time.

03:10.690 --> 03:11.524
Mom…

03:48.937 --> 03:49.771
Mom.

03:57.362 --> 03:58.613
Mom!

04:00.365 --> 04:01.199
Mom!

04:07.080 --> 04:08.164
Mom!

04:09.332 --> 04:11.209
Mom!

04:11.918 --> 04:14.212
Mom!

04:14.796 --> 04:16.589
Come ashore quickly!

04:17.215 --> 04:19.592
Why are you always the last one
to come ashore?

04:22.679 --> 04:23.680
Seriously!

04:24.389 --> 04:26.266
Is your daughter an abalone or something?

04:26.766 --> 04:28.184
Why did you go back in?

04:28.726 --> 04:31.020
Did you go back in there just to annoy me?

04:32.021 --> 04:34.399
Mom!

04:34.482 --> 04:37.777
Seaweed flourishes in the spring.
That willful soul won't leave the sea.

04:38.361 --> 04:39.320
Ae-sun.

04:39.404 --> 04:40.655
Stop shouting for your mom.

04:40.738 --> 04:43.199
Take a look at Mr. Yang's cheeks instead!

04:45.159 --> 04:46.953
It's just sunburn!

04:47.036 --> 04:51.457
Why is Ae-sun the only one who can't see
his heart burning in the spring sunlight?

04:53.376 --> 04:55.003
Seriously, think about it.

04:55.086 --> 05:00.341
If a haenyeo's daughter wed a fishmonger,
wouldn't she own the whole sea of Jeju?

05:00.425 --> 05:01.926
You're so annoying.

05:06.055 --> 05:07.515
There she goes.

05:09.851 --> 05:11.060
Did you get slapped?

05:11.144 --> 05:12.645
Why are your cheeks always red?

05:14.647 --> 05:16.316
Gwan-sik got rejected again.

05:25.616 --> 05:28.745
She should've given birth
to an abalone instead of me.

05:30.121 --> 05:31.247
Mr. Yang.

05:31.748 --> 05:34.375
I have two conches. There you go.

05:35.168 --> 05:37.128
Come on, give me a good price.

05:37.920 --> 05:38.755
Yes, ma'am.

05:39.714 --> 05:43.092
Did you even scoop red seaweed
off the Dragon King's throat?

05:43.176 --> 05:46.054
Greed kills a haenyeo,
not her lack of knowledge of the sea.

05:46.137 --> 05:49.182
Greed is what gets a haenyeo.

05:49.849 --> 05:52.310
How is Granny Hallim doing?

05:53.227 --> 05:54.729
Her breathing isn't improving.

05:54.812 --> 05:57.315
Our nets are the lifeline
for the sick haenyeo,

05:57.398 --> 05:59.359
so let's share and save her life.

06:00.026 --> 06:01.652
Is there only seaweed here?

06:02.445 --> 06:04.155
My mom told me to get some abalones.

06:04.238 --> 06:05.531
They're in there. Find them.

06:06.032 --> 06:08.034
Spring abalones are as tiny as rat poo.

06:08.618 --> 06:10.036
There's nothing to eat.

06:12.955 --> 06:15.666
Why don't you just give her everything?
Go ahead!

06:15.750 --> 06:17.627
There she goes again, freaking out.

06:17.710 --> 06:19.253
Granny Hallim has three sons.

06:19.337 --> 06:21.506
Why is it on us to feed her?

06:21.589 --> 06:25.385
Would I risk my life every day
diving to the underworld just to feed her?

06:25.885 --> 06:30.723
I sell my breath to catch abalones
to feed my own kids, not some granny!

06:31.557 --> 06:33.184
You think you're so clever?

06:33.267 --> 06:35.144
Who taught you how to dive?

06:35.228 --> 06:37.605
Who do you owe
for being able to feed your kids?

06:37.688 --> 06:40.942
All of your families have hungry kids
waiting open-mouthed,

06:41.025 --> 06:42.985
and you wanna take care
of a sick old woman?

06:43.569 --> 06:45.488
There's no way
I'm giving my abalones away.

06:45.988 --> 06:47.323
The thought alone angers me.

06:47.990 --> 06:48.825
Count properly!

06:49.742 --> 06:51.202
How did she get sick?

06:51.911 --> 06:53.955
We'd do the same for you if you got sick.

06:55.081 --> 06:56.541
I'm not going to get sick.

06:56.624 --> 06:59.085
Haenyeo live and die together.
We can't do it alone.

06:59.168 --> 07:02.130
If you're all so giving,
why live in service of the Dragon King?

07:03.923 --> 07:08.052
You got a new husband for a better life,
but you're even more willful now.

07:09.762 --> 07:12.056
You take care of a new husband
who leeches off you,

07:12.140 --> 07:14.183
but you won't share
with the master haenyeo?

07:14.267 --> 07:16.394
When we both fled here
and lived like beggars,

07:16.477 --> 07:17.979
who taught us how to dive?

07:18.563 --> 07:22.108
If you don't appreciate Granny Hallim,
you're worth less than a saury.

07:23.276 --> 07:26.612
So did your husband's mouth droop
'cause you're better than a saury?

07:27.321 --> 07:29.073
He slept in the cold!

07:29.157 --> 07:31.784
Your husband's mouth drooped
because he couldn't eat.

07:31.868 --> 07:34.287
Yet you run your mouth
like you're special?

07:34.954 --> 07:37.707
Even if you're right,
someone worthy should say those things.

07:37.790 --> 07:40.376
Your kids have different surnames.
How worthy are you?

07:40.460 --> 07:42.044
-Enough!
-Gyeong-ja!

07:42.128 --> 07:44.547
-Come on!
-I knew it.

07:45.298 --> 07:47.550
We can't go home until they fight.

07:56.225 --> 07:57.268
What? Not again!

07:58.186 --> 08:00.146
What the hell… You damn bitch!

08:00.229 --> 08:02.857
Crap! Damn you!

08:02.940 --> 08:05.943
What are you… You damn bitch!

08:06.694 --> 08:07.612
Damn it!

08:08.154 --> 08:11.407
I shouldn't have brought her
when I fled here.

08:11.491 --> 08:12.617
What a waste!

08:12.700 --> 08:14.368
So why poke a puffer fish?

08:14.952 --> 08:17.580
Why mess with someone
who lives out of spite?

08:18.289 --> 08:20.458
What a damn waste!

08:20.541 --> 08:23.294
Go home and kick your leech of a husband.

08:23.377 --> 08:25.463
Don't kick someone else's stuff.

08:46.484 --> 08:47.818
Is an abalone your daughter?

08:47.902 --> 08:51.155
I got an award,
but all you do is look at abalones.

08:51.239 --> 08:52.698
Why would you write a poem?

08:52.782 --> 08:55.326
Does it get us an abalone or a conch?

08:55.868 --> 08:57.370
Come on, give it a read!

08:57.453 --> 08:59.497
I was runner-up in the writing contest.

08:59.580 --> 09:01.582
Go show it to your grandmother.

09:01.666 --> 09:03.417
The Oh family loves scholars.

09:06.212 --> 09:09.757
Show them and demand,
"Help me get through school."

09:09.840 --> 09:11.259
Grandma doesn't like me.

09:12.176 --> 09:14.178
She says I look more like you every day,

09:14.804 --> 09:16.264
so she doesn't want to see me.

09:16.764 --> 09:18.641
Go to your home and eat there.

09:18.724 --> 09:20.810
I told you I'm eating here.

09:20.893 --> 09:23.145
Go! Your stepdad will be back soon.

09:24.105 --> 09:25.147
So what if he is?

09:25.231 --> 09:28.859
Can't I even eat the conch
and red seaweed my mom collected?

09:29.777 --> 09:33.030
Oh's daughter should eat with the Ohs.
Why beg for food here?

09:33.114 --> 09:34.824
Uncle doesn't let me have croakers.

09:37.827 --> 09:38.703
He doesn't?

09:38.786 --> 09:43.207
He says Oh Jong-gu always comes last
because I get full marks and win awards.

09:43.291 --> 09:45.793
He says I take all the eldest son's luck.

09:47.295 --> 09:49.422
It's not that I want to eat croaker.

09:50.756 --> 09:53.676
It's just not fair
that he's like that with food.

09:54.719 --> 09:56.345
I don't want to eat at all.

09:57.471 --> 09:58.472
While I eat,

09:59.140 --> 10:00.349
I keep choking.

10:01.976 --> 10:04.061
Can't I just live here?

10:04.687 --> 10:05.605
Can't I?

10:06.522 --> 10:07.523
No chance?

10:10.234 --> 10:12.111
-Never?
-Why would you choke?

10:12.194 --> 10:13.237
You did nothing wrong.

10:13.321 --> 10:15.615
Who's gonna like you
if you choke while eating?

10:17.825 --> 10:18.951
Go.

10:19.035 --> 10:19.869
I said go!

10:19.952 --> 10:21.329
Go earn your own love.

10:21.412 --> 10:22.955
Go find your own food.

10:23.039 --> 10:26.000
Hey, you're here again, Sun-ae.

10:26.083 --> 10:27.376
It's Ae-sun!

10:27.460 --> 10:28.794
Are you stupid?

10:28.878 --> 10:29.712
Ae-sun.

10:31.005 --> 10:32.381
Are you staying for dinner?

10:32.465 --> 10:34.133
No, I won't be eating.

10:48.814 --> 10:50.024
That rascal.

10:56.113 --> 10:57.448
Here, Dad.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.619
She's like a thorn in my side.

11:03.454 --> 11:05.539
I heard smoking can kill
even the Dragon King.

11:06.040 --> 11:10.378
It's a death wish for a haenyeo to smoke
when her life depends on breathing.

11:18.052 --> 11:20.012
Why don't you just bring her here?

11:21.389 --> 11:24.850
I still think
you should just bring her here.

11:26.936 --> 11:29.522
For someone with nothing,
you're so damn nosy.

11:29.605 --> 11:32.066
Even if we take her in,
do we have a house or any money?

11:32.566 --> 11:34.652
There's no room
in this little thatched rental.

11:34.735 --> 11:38.197
How can you stop a child
from snuggling into its mother?

11:39.115 --> 11:41.784
What if I take her in?
Will we raise her instead of cows?

11:42.284 --> 11:44.286
Or make her look after her stepsiblings?

11:44.370 --> 11:46.455
Blood is thicker than water.

11:47.415 --> 11:51.502
You insist on staying here
so you can see your precious daughter.

11:51.585 --> 11:55.005
And that kid walks all the way here
every chance she gets.

11:55.506 --> 11:59.301
She's dying to see her mom.
What good is keeping her registered there?

11:59.802 --> 12:02.054
It's just making you both suffer.

12:02.138 --> 12:03.431
At least they have money.

12:03.931 --> 12:05.599
She can finish her studies there.

12:06.183 --> 12:07.476
Why make a girl study?

12:07.560 --> 12:09.186
It will only cause her more stress.

12:11.355 --> 12:14.900
I heard that haenyeo start learning
how to dive in their early teens.

12:14.984 --> 12:18.571
Would you say that about your daughter?
Would you make your daughter dive?

12:23.659 --> 12:26.704
These damn island women
jump at every word that's said.

12:27.455 --> 12:28.998
I will never let her dive.

12:29.623 --> 12:32.042
It's better to be born a cow
than a haenyeo.

12:32.668 --> 12:36.130
I slog my guts out all day
and still have nothing to show for it.

12:36.213 --> 12:37.214
It's discouraging.

12:37.298 --> 12:39.842
So what's the point
of coming to live here?

12:40.509 --> 12:42.720
That kind kid would be nothing
but a maid here.

12:43.512 --> 12:44.555
I'll throw this away.

12:47.057 --> 12:48.851
Reading it will only hurt you.

12:50.019 --> 12:51.729
Why are you folding it?

12:51.812 --> 12:54.273
Why would you fold the runner-up's work?

13:00.154 --> 13:01.947
It's best not to read it.

13:16.003 --> 13:17.463
GYONGGI NOODLE

13:24.804 --> 13:27.223
It's how you write "stupid idiot."

13:45.282 --> 13:47.368
Does he wanna die or what?

13:55.793 --> 13:56.919
I only bought five.

13:57.795 --> 13:58.963
One of them is free.

13:59.046 --> 13:59.964
Did your mom say so?

14:04.093 --> 14:05.094
Did she say that?

14:06.220 --> 14:09.598
There are six people in the family,
but you only ever buy five.

14:10.099 --> 14:12.017
Do you make a fortune selling fish?

14:12.518 --> 14:13.519
Nosy little brat.

14:15.604 --> 14:17.022
That little punk.

14:17.690 --> 14:18.524
Look here!

14:22.736 --> 14:25.281
Ae-sun,
you need to soak the cauldron first.

14:26.407 --> 14:28.367
What? Why come here?

14:42.715 --> 14:44.383
There! Damn croakers!

14:45.885 --> 14:47.887
Look here! Are you out of your mind?

14:47.970 --> 14:49.388
Where do you think you are?

14:49.471 --> 14:50.598
Are you saving croakers?

14:50.681 --> 14:51.599
What are you saying?

14:51.682 --> 14:53.183
Making a fortune off croakers?

14:53.934 --> 14:57.354
Mother, she's also a daughter
in the Oh family.

14:57.438 --> 14:59.690
Surely, she resembles her father!

15:00.733 --> 15:01.775
Don't be like that.

15:02.276 --> 15:03.235
Please don't.

15:04.236 --> 15:05.446
Your son!

15:05.529 --> 15:09.450
Your big brother is shedding
tears of blood from his grave!

15:09.533 --> 15:11.368
You're the bad luck that killed him!

15:11.452 --> 15:13.746
How dare you mention my brother's name!

15:17.833 --> 15:20.169
What's up with you?
Are you possessed or something?

15:21.378 --> 15:23.547
Is it my fault
your brother lived a short life?

15:24.381 --> 15:28.010
You ought to be sorry
for giving her a father with a short life.

15:31.138 --> 15:33.432
My daughter! I'm taking her back.

15:37.937 --> 15:39.355
Screw washing dishes.

15:40.814 --> 15:41.982
Unbelievable!

16:00.292 --> 16:04.505
I'm glad he didn't feed me any croakers.
Now I get to live with you.

16:05.631 --> 16:06.924
Do you like me?

16:10.844 --> 16:12.137
Why do you like me?

16:12.221 --> 16:13.472
Because you're my mom.

16:14.139 --> 16:14.974
Goodness.

16:15.849 --> 16:19.103
I like you because you're my mom.
Isn't that obvious?

16:19.812 --> 16:22.106
If you like me, then grow up fast.

16:23.440 --> 16:24.441
Grow up fast

16:25.651 --> 16:27.444
and give me 100 hwan every day.

16:28.070 --> 16:28.904
You read it?

16:39.498 --> 16:40.791
"Stupid Abalone"

16:40.874 --> 16:43.168
by Oh Ae-sun from class 3-8.

16:44.378 --> 16:46.505
Abalone every day.

16:47.006 --> 16:49.174
Abalone when it's stormy and gray.

16:49.925 --> 16:51.885
Abalone over her daughter I'd say.

16:52.720 --> 16:55.472
I hope to see you come ashore soon.

16:56.015 --> 16:58.475
Why don't I see you when I see the moon?

16:59.893 --> 17:01.854
Are there no abalones about,

17:02.312 --> 17:04.314
Are you out of breath
searching for abalones,

17:04.857 --> 17:06.984
Your daughter worries, starts to fret.

17:07.067 --> 17:10.279
Catching no abalones makes Mom sweat.

17:13.615 --> 17:15.701
The 100 hwan she earns
from selling an abalone.

17:15.784 --> 17:18.579
I want to pay it so I can buy her day.

17:19.580 --> 17:21.123
My mom whose back aches,

17:21.665 --> 17:23.208
my mom who coughs.

17:24.460 --> 17:28.088
With 100 hwan every day,
I want to let her rest.

17:39.600 --> 17:40.559
Do you have one?

17:41.351 --> 17:42.603
A daughter like this?

17:44.229 --> 17:45.731
How did I get so lucky?

17:54.114 --> 17:55.741
Good grief.

18:11.715 --> 18:15.010
Give me 100 hwan every day
so I don't have to dive.

18:17.513 --> 18:21.725
I also want to spend the whole day
looking at my precious child.

18:23.685 --> 18:26.522
-It was good enough to come second, right?
-Those blind fools.

18:28.023 --> 18:28.941
Was it that bad?

18:29.441 --> 18:30.818
Second place for that?

18:31.735 --> 18:32.986
It should've come first!

18:53.173 --> 18:56.760
Don't mistreat her. If you do,
you'll be kicked out, not her.

18:56.844 --> 19:01.056
You may not be lucky with husbands,
but it seems like you are with your child.

19:01.890 --> 19:03.016
This little rascal.

19:03.684 --> 19:05.269
She's the biggest rascal.

19:06.019 --> 19:07.729
Where else would you find
a rascal like this?

19:08.313 --> 19:10.440
I wouldn't mind a rascal like that.

19:14.862 --> 19:17.156
My parents were deep in debt.

19:17.906 --> 19:19.825
I had to nurse my first husband.

19:20.534 --> 19:22.411
And the new one is a freeloader.

19:22.494 --> 19:24.663
I was destined to be a porter.

19:25.455 --> 19:28.167
Everyone just wants to ride on my back…

19:30.252 --> 19:34.006
but this kid, as tiny as a bean,
keeps getting off my back.

19:35.132 --> 19:37.134
and offering to help carry my load.

19:42.556 --> 19:43.974
That's why she's a rascal.

19:45.601 --> 19:47.853
She gets to me the most,
so she's a rascal.

19:48.353 --> 19:49.479
Just wait and see.

19:50.522 --> 19:54.359
That rascal will take care
of your ancestral rites after you're gone.

19:54.443 --> 19:58.822
A shameless mother like me
couldn't possibly ask for such things.

20:02.242 --> 20:05.495
I won't let my precious child
carry a funeral palanquin.

20:06.371 --> 20:09.124
I'll see her
in a dignitary palanquin later.

20:12.628 --> 20:15.464
Even Confucius
couldn't write as well as her.

20:16.173 --> 20:17.299
Ae-sun

20:18.550 --> 20:21.261
is sure to make it big one day.

20:27.392 --> 20:29.519
THE FIFTH NATIONAL ASSEMBLY ELECTION

20:33.982 --> 20:37.611
Thanks to my daughter,
I get to hold a big title.

20:38.987 --> 20:41.657
You're the vice president,
so I'm the vice president's mom.

20:41.740 --> 20:43.784
Should I hand out rice cakes?

20:43.867 --> 20:45.911
I don't wanna be the vice president!

20:46.453 --> 20:47.996
The fishing co-op is the same.

20:48.080 --> 20:50.666
The deputy chief
is just as important as the chief.

20:50.749 --> 20:53.543
If everyone wants to be chief,
who will be deputy?

20:53.961 --> 20:56.255
Normally, the deputy has more power
than the chief.

20:56.338 --> 20:59.007
Who on earth wants to become a deputy?

20:59.091 --> 21:01.635
I've never even had a chance
to be a group leader.

21:02.219 --> 21:05.514
I want to write in the family records
that you were the vice president.

21:05.597 --> 21:08.141
Don't write it down! Absolutely not!

21:08.809 --> 21:11.520
Actually, Oh Ae-sun was supposed
to be the president.

21:11.603 --> 21:13.563
Right. I'm sure you think she was.

21:13.647 --> 21:15.899
You should at least treat her
like a president.

21:16.400 --> 21:20.195
Oh Ae-sun got 37 votes,
and Lee Man-ki got 28 votes.

21:20.279 --> 21:22.197
Why is Lee Man-ki the president?

21:22.281 --> 21:26.201
Why am I the vice president?
Why did they steal my president role?

21:26.910 --> 21:27.744
"Steal"?

21:28.328 --> 21:31.331
CLASS PRESIDENT ELECTION
OH AE-SUN, LEE MAN-KI

21:31.915 --> 21:34.334
Don't you think you're being selfish?

21:34.418 --> 21:36.461
But I'm the one who got 37 votes.

21:39.339 --> 21:41.466
You have some nerve keeping this up.

21:42.968 --> 21:46.179
Didn't you eat the cream buns
Man-ki's father gave out?

21:47.222 --> 21:51.018
Didn't you scrub the floor
with the wax he provided?

21:52.185 --> 21:53.937
I'm still the one who got 37 votes.

21:56.857 --> 22:01.069
Those 37 who took everything
but didn't vote for Man-ki are unethical.

22:02.237 --> 22:04.740
But wherever it may be,
a person at the top

22:04.823 --> 22:08.827
should be competent both mentally
and financially, you know?

22:09.453 --> 22:11.079
I'm the one who got 37 votes.

22:11.163 --> 22:12.706
So what if you got 37 votes?

22:12.789 --> 22:14.708
Do your 37 votes matter now?

22:14.791 --> 22:18.128
In real life,
37 votes don't mean anything!

22:18.211 --> 22:19.838
Between you and Man-ki,

22:21.173 --> 22:24.676
there's something that goes
beyond just nine votes, okay?

22:30.223 --> 22:33.810
It looks bad to be dragged down,
but stepping down preserves your dignity.

22:34.394 --> 22:35.896
Sacrifice for the greater good.

22:36.396 --> 22:37.856
The one who loses wins.

22:41.068 --> 22:43.195
The one who loses loses.

22:43.278 --> 22:45.822
The one who loses just loses!

22:45.906 --> 22:47.699
Why am I the vice president?

22:47.783 --> 22:49.034
Why?

22:49.117 --> 22:50.410
Hey, quit it!

22:50.494 --> 22:52.287
Why did you run for something like this?

22:52.371 --> 22:54.748
Haven't you seen
the election posters on the wall?

22:54.831 --> 22:57.167
You could lose everything
if you love titles.

22:57.250 --> 22:58.877
I should be the president!

22:59.461 --> 23:01.338
Give it back to me!

23:23.777 --> 23:27.614
You caused a scene and stormed off
as if you'd never see us again.

23:27.697 --> 23:28.573
You know what?

23:28.657 --> 23:30.409
I'm speaking honestly here.

23:30.951 --> 23:32.702
I think this family needs to wake up.

23:33.203 --> 23:37.457
You're a daughter-in-law, not a cow.
How will you plow this field alone?

23:37.958 --> 23:39.042
I have no money.

23:43.588 --> 23:45.757
You should leave. Go now!

23:46.550 --> 23:49.177
If my mother-in-law finds out, I'm dead.

23:49.261 --> 23:50.679
You can just run away,

23:51.638 --> 23:54.391
but I have to stay with the Ohs
for the rest of my life.

23:54.474 --> 23:57.269
I'll wrap this up quickly
and harvest the sesame for you.

23:57.352 --> 23:58.979
I told you I have no money!

24:00.480 --> 24:01.356
I have nothing.

24:02.274 --> 24:03.859
Search me. See if I have anything.

24:03.942 --> 24:05.485
No. You have something.

24:06.236 --> 24:07.070
I know you do.

24:08.113 --> 24:10.615
-Right?
-Just take me instead.

24:10.699 --> 24:12.868
I'm dirt poor. I've got nothing at all.

24:12.951 --> 24:14.786
No, I'm not talking about money.

24:16.246 --> 24:17.330
You know,

24:17.414 --> 24:19.374
what I want is…

24:21.376 --> 24:22.419
that thing.

24:25.589 --> 24:27.007
No. Not in a million years.

24:27.799 --> 24:29.217
Will it wear out?

24:29.759 --> 24:33.138
I'll plow the field
and harvest the sesame for you!

24:33.221 --> 24:35.348
Can't you at least lend that to a servant?

24:35.432 --> 24:38.351
Absolutely not!
I cherish it too much to use it myself.

24:40.061 --> 24:43.315
I swear I will plow this whole field
in two days.

24:43.857 --> 24:47.277
Think of it as borrowing a cow
to plow the field for a few days.

24:50.697 --> 24:55.118
Who lends their wedding jewelry?
Why didn't you get one when you remarried?

24:56.286 --> 24:57.621
Come on. You know me!

24:57.704 --> 24:59.414
I can plow better than a cow.

25:27.067 --> 25:28.109
STUPID ABALONE

25:28.193 --> 25:30.529
THE LOYAL LEE FAMILY
BY LEE MAN-KI FROM CLASS 3-8

25:30.612 --> 25:32.113
MY FATHER
IS LOYAL TO THE COUNTRY!

25:32.155 --> 25:34.324
Loyalty, loyalty. What endless flattery!

25:34.866 --> 25:36.076
A kid wrote this?

25:36.576 --> 25:38.870
This homework is for kids,
not their parents.

25:40.705 --> 25:41.540
Hey.

25:42.415 --> 25:45.502
Isn't it obvious
that this one should be the winner?

25:47.045 --> 25:48.880
So what if it's in a gold frame?

25:48.964 --> 25:52.008
What's inside is on a different level.

25:53.426 --> 25:54.636
I get it.

25:55.178 --> 25:57.180
The general's son gets first place.

25:57.681 --> 25:59.849
The general's son gets to be president.

25:59.933 --> 26:02.102
How disgusting.

26:02.602 --> 26:04.479
It's such a disgrace!

26:06.147 --> 26:07.232
Do you happen to be

26:07.941 --> 26:09.192
Ae-sun's aunt?

26:12.612 --> 26:13.446
Take a seat.

26:13.530 --> 26:14.364
Thank you.

26:23.164 --> 26:25.000
MASTERMIND OF THE 3.15 ELECTION FRAUD

26:32.465 --> 26:33.300
Actually,

26:34.426 --> 26:36.094
I'm Ae-sun's mom,

26:36.928 --> 26:37.804
not her aunt.

26:39.097 --> 26:40.557
Right. I see.

26:41.349 --> 26:43.810
Ae-sun has a mom too.

26:44.561 --> 26:45.395
Sure.

26:46.187 --> 26:49.566
I've been busy making ends meet,
so I couldn't visit you.

26:51.359 --> 26:54.654
I brought some rice cakes
for you to share with the class.

26:56.865 --> 26:58.033
Oh, there was no need.

26:58.783 --> 27:00.994
Actually, I did need to.

27:02.454 --> 27:04.122
PRESIDENT: MAN-KI
VICE PRESIDENT: AE-SUN

27:04.205 --> 27:06.666
To celebrate my kid,
who deserves to be the president.

27:10.503 --> 27:12.672
The runner-up
who deserved the first place.

27:16.509 --> 27:18.011
What did he say?

27:18.511 --> 27:20.055
Am I gonna be the president?

27:20.138 --> 27:21.264
Do I get it back?

27:23.725 --> 27:25.018
Did you get mad again?

27:25.101 --> 27:27.562
Did you cause a scene again
like you did at Grandma's?

27:28.146 --> 27:29.147
You bet I did.

27:29.898 --> 27:31.900
I made sure to shut him up for good.

27:33.818 --> 27:34.694
All right, then.

27:34.778 --> 27:36.571
I'll have the rice cakes with the kids.

27:37.113 --> 27:38.615
I left my child in your care,

27:39.491 --> 27:41.951
but I was too busy making a living, so…

27:42.035 --> 27:43.286
But you know,

27:43.370 --> 27:45.080
there are 70 students in the class,

27:46.206 --> 27:48.541
and every one of them eats like a pig.

27:48.625 --> 27:51.169
I'm not sure
if there's enough to go around.

27:52.587 --> 27:56.007
I'm sure all parents feels the same when
they leave their children with someone.

27:57.008 --> 28:00.053
Please take good care of my daughter.

28:00.845 --> 28:03.973
There's nothing much I can do.
It's all up to her.

28:04.849 --> 28:06.935
The rice cakes might be a bit lacking,

28:07.018 --> 28:11.648
but all parents want their children
to be loved more than anyone else.

28:14.067 --> 28:15.026
If I could,

28:15.527 --> 28:17.570
I'd have brought a whole cow.

28:18.113 --> 28:19.322
These are just to…

28:21.408 --> 28:23.118
keep your feet warm.

28:23.201 --> 28:25.120
You didn't have to do this.

28:25.203 --> 28:27.872
They are for keeping your feet warm.

28:30.834 --> 28:32.085
They are made from nylon.

28:56.818 --> 28:58.027
At least she's respectful.

28:58.111 --> 29:00.363
THANK YOU ALWAYS
FROM OH AE-SUN'S MOTHER

29:04.284 --> 29:06.369
This is making me uncomfortable.

29:07.078 --> 29:09.330
Did she stop by the bank, or what?

29:09.831 --> 29:11.166
Crisp new bills.

29:12.834 --> 29:14.794
Why did you dress up like this?

29:14.878 --> 29:16.463
I didn't want to reek of salt.

29:16.963 --> 29:19.132
They say to show teachers
the utmost respect.

29:19.632 --> 29:22.093
I couldn't bring rice cakes
while smelling so salty.

29:22.677 --> 29:26.139
Make sure to listen to your teacher
so you become a good person.

29:26.806 --> 29:30.477
It'd be nice to live like your teacher,
sitting at a desk and writing stuff.

29:31.269 --> 29:33.396
He won't let me be president, will he?

29:34.606 --> 29:37.025
Did he ask you to buy something?
Like a broom?

29:38.693 --> 29:40.487
For mental and financial competence?

29:41.863 --> 29:44.574
I tried it for a few days,
and vice president is better.

29:45.200 --> 29:47.660
The only difference
is the "vice" in the front.

29:47.744 --> 29:49.454
It's practically the same thing.

29:49.537 --> 29:53.041
I can't lead the greeting to the teacher,
but it feels like I am.

29:53.625 --> 29:55.293
When Lee Man-ki does it,

29:55.794 --> 29:57.670
I also do it in my mind.

29:59.380 --> 30:01.090
Vice president is just better.

30:04.552 --> 30:05.512
Ae-sun.

30:06.596 --> 30:09.766
I am the poor one, not you.

30:10.475 --> 30:11.309
Don't hang back.

30:12.060 --> 30:14.562
Live your life to the fullest.

30:16.648 --> 30:18.399
You shouldn't hang back either.

30:18.483 --> 30:21.820
When I grow up, the first thing I'll do…

30:29.869 --> 30:32.831
-What's gotten into you?
-I want to live for a long time.

30:33.748 --> 30:36.209
Our eldest daughter says
the first thing she'll do

30:36.960 --> 30:38.711
is buy me a pearl necklace.

30:38.795 --> 30:40.421
I need to try it on.

30:40.505 --> 30:41.756
Oh dear.

30:41.840 --> 30:43.174
In what lifetime?

30:43.800 --> 30:45.510
Kids grow up in a heartbeat.

30:46.511 --> 30:48.847
I'll put on the pearl necklace in no time.

30:49.472 --> 30:53.393
Kids aren't the only ones growing quickly.
We'll grow old fast too.

30:53.476 --> 30:55.436
I was watching the news earlier.

30:55.520 --> 30:58.022
They say the average lifespan
in Korea is just 52.

30:58.523 --> 30:59.774
I'm going to outlive that.

31:00.316 --> 31:02.694
I'll keep enjoying my life
into my 60s and 70s.

31:03.403 --> 31:07.574
When that time comes,
this hardship will seem like nothing.

31:07.657 --> 31:09.909
Then I'll laugh it off.

31:20.420 --> 31:21.963
I don't remember quitting smoking.

31:22.046 --> 31:23.256
Quit starting today.

31:26.301 --> 31:29.554
Hey, come on.

31:30.221 --> 31:32.974
-Whoa.
-Damn it.

31:45.737 --> 31:47.363
Spring is just so short.

31:48.531 --> 31:52.660
Just when I think it has arrived,
its blossom festival fades in an instant,

31:57.749 --> 31:59.751
so heartlessly.

32:20.271 --> 32:22.023
Enough with your tenacity!

32:22.106 --> 32:24.984
How can you keep diving
when you can barely breathe?

32:25.985 --> 32:27.779
Don't say pointless things.

32:27.862 --> 32:30.073
Let me live long enough
to need diapers again.

32:30.156 --> 32:33.284
Your chest is so bad you reek of blood,
but you still dive?

32:33.368 --> 32:35.203
You might as well dive with a coffin!

32:35.286 --> 32:37.664
To die out here or in the water,
it's all the same.

32:37.747 --> 32:41.709
Hey! Can't you see him standing there
waiting for you outside?

32:41.793 --> 32:45.171
He's standing there in black
waiting for you.

32:45.254 --> 32:46.089
Go into the water,

32:46.172 --> 32:48.341
and the Grim Reaper over there

32:48.424 --> 32:51.803
will stare down at you like this
in the water.

32:51.886 --> 32:54.973
If I were scared of him,
I wouldn't have dived for a living.

32:55.056 --> 32:56.933
A haenyeo's life depends on luck.

32:57.016 --> 32:59.894
I've come close to death
in deep blue water countless times.

33:02.063 --> 33:04.732
Are you doing this
because you might starve your kids?

33:05.441 --> 33:08.152
Gwang-rye! Haenyeo live and die together.

33:08.236 --> 33:10.279
We are going to feed you, so--

33:10.363 --> 33:13.449
I'd rather die earning a penny
than die begging.

33:14.033 --> 33:17.245
I can’t die until I leave
at least a penny more for my kids.

33:17.870 --> 33:19.163
No, I won't.

33:19.247 --> 33:21.332
It doesn't take much to turn into a ghost.

33:21.416 --> 33:25.253
Your fear of regret makes you resentful.
Your willfulness will make you a ghost.

33:26.004 --> 33:28.256
Ghosts don't scare me. My children do.

33:28.339 --> 33:31.342
If I'm living on borrowed time,
I'll earn what I can until I die

33:31.426 --> 33:33.386
to keep my kids fed in this world.

33:36.889 --> 33:39.475
Way to go!
She can't dive without her diving suit!

33:39.559 --> 33:42.687
That rascal.
I shouldn't have brought her back.

33:50.570 --> 33:53.197
OH AE-SUN IS YANG GWAN-SIK'S WIFE
AE-SUN IS GETTING MARRIED

33:58.119 --> 33:59.287
Am I a beggar?

34:00.121 --> 34:01.414
Am I?

34:15.887 --> 34:18.806
Leave my mom alone!

34:18.890 --> 34:21.309
At least leave my mom alone!

34:22.602 --> 34:23.978
Why are you doing this?

34:24.062 --> 34:27.190
Why do you take innocent people
whenever you want?

34:31.152 --> 34:32.820
You should go easy!

34:33.362 --> 34:35.364
You should go easy!

34:35.448 --> 34:37.950
You should go easy on Mom!

34:38.576 --> 34:41.412
She's spent her whole life working hard

34:42.580 --> 34:44.540
and has never been on a plane.

34:45.917 --> 34:47.251
I was going to get her

34:48.127 --> 34:49.754
a pearl necklace

34:50.421 --> 34:52.882
and fly her on a plane.

34:54.175 --> 34:55.176
Why?

34:57.220 --> 34:58.930
Why?

35:01.766 --> 35:03.184
Why?

35:08.481 --> 35:09.732
Cat got your tongue?

35:10.233 --> 35:13.528
You're as quiet as a mouse!
Why aren't you saying anything?

35:14.529 --> 35:15.655
What is it this time?

35:16.197 --> 35:17.532
What?

35:18.366 --> 35:19.200
Show me!

35:20.618 --> 35:22.245
-Can I come closer?
-Come here!

35:27.875 --> 35:31.087
You think I wouldn't be able to eat
croakers or mackerels without you?

35:34.006 --> 35:35.633
It's meat, not fish.

35:35.716 --> 35:38.719
People don't even share
precious meat with their in-laws.

35:40.388 --> 35:41.681
Are you dumb?

35:42.431 --> 35:44.267
Is there something wrong with you?

35:44.767 --> 35:46.269
If you cry, you'll be hungry.

35:46.769 --> 35:47.937
Are you pitying me?

35:48.646 --> 35:50.606
Is that why you keep bringing me food?

35:51.107 --> 35:53.276
If it was out of pity, I'd feed a beggar.

35:55.236 --> 35:56.696
You little punk.

35:58.614 --> 35:59.740
I am

36:01.075 --> 36:02.160
older than you.

36:13.212 --> 36:15.756
Bring me beef
instead of chicken every day.

36:16.299 --> 36:17.758
I still won't marry you.

36:18.342 --> 36:19.343
I didn't ask you to.

36:37.612 --> 36:39.322
Please, God, she must live on.

36:40.990 --> 36:43.409
How could you take her away from her kids?

36:48.164 --> 36:48.998
Mother.

36:52.126 --> 36:53.044
Mother.

37:01.886 --> 37:03.888
Could you please come with me?

37:04.764 --> 37:06.349
I'm scared to go on my own.

37:22.365 --> 37:23.699
What is it?

37:27.620 --> 37:29.038
Is that you, Mom?

37:52.937 --> 37:55.273
I feel like I got a golden axe
instead of my own.

37:56.357 --> 37:58.442
Am I just an iron axe, then?

38:01.320 --> 38:02.697
Did you go somewhere?

38:03.698 --> 38:05.783
You could've given them to me tomorrow.

38:06.325 --> 38:08.327
Your siblings would
take them all tomorrow.

38:09.203 --> 38:11.163
You can sell them for 100 hwan each.

38:14.333 --> 38:16.419
It's worth 1,000 hwan if you eat them.

38:26.512 --> 38:27.346
Ae-sun.

38:28.681 --> 38:29.890
As soon as I die…

38:32.435 --> 38:33.561
leave this place.

38:34.562 --> 38:37.023
Go to your uncle and beg for your life.

38:38.316 --> 38:40.318
Don't stay here
and be a maid for the Yeoms.

38:42.778 --> 38:44.739
Leave this place, no matter what.

38:45.489 --> 38:46.324
Promise me.

38:47.533 --> 38:48.367
I won't promise.

38:49.327 --> 38:50.328
Stop talking.

38:53.789 --> 38:56.917
Live with your uncle,
and have him walk you down the aisle.

38:57.626 --> 39:00.880
If you get married
without a father figure, I will cry.

39:00.963 --> 39:03.466
I said I wouldn't promise.
Why are you still talking?

39:05.760 --> 39:07.762
I won't rest unless you promise.

39:08.971 --> 39:10.222
Dad died.

39:11.015 --> 39:12.224
You're dying too.

39:13.434 --> 39:14.769
Why is everyone dying?

39:16.479 --> 39:18.689
Then why did you give birth to me?

39:20.775 --> 39:21.609
Ae-sun.

39:22.610 --> 39:25.696
In the end,
we all end up living as orphans.

39:26.697 --> 39:28.282
Even though parents die first,

39:29.241 --> 39:30.534
their children carry on.

39:30.618 --> 39:31.869
Life goes on and on.

39:32.787 --> 39:35.247
There will be tougher days in your life.

39:36.916 --> 39:38.959
One day, life might get so tough

39:39.543 --> 39:41.879
that you feel like you can't go on--

39:41.962 --> 39:43.547
I told you to stop talking!

39:44.131 --> 39:45.091
I won't promise.

39:45.966 --> 39:47.885
I'm not going to eat abalone.

39:54.350 --> 39:55.434
My precious little one.

39:57.436 --> 39:58.771
When will you grow up?

40:02.024 --> 40:04.777
The eldest daughter
heard her mom's last words

40:05.319 --> 40:06.612
at the age of ten.

40:07.613 --> 40:10.658
Sleep, sleep

40:10.741 --> 40:13.285
Rock to sleep

40:13.369 --> 40:18.374
Sleep, sleep, rock to sleep

40:18.457 --> 40:23.796
My baby sleeps well

40:25.047 --> 40:27.091
Sleep quickly

40:27.174 --> 40:29.301
Sleep quickly

40:31.095 --> 40:35.641
A black dog walks away

40:36.767 --> 40:40.729
A black dog walks this way

40:43.023 --> 40:47.445
Come help my baby sleep

40:48.362 --> 40:52.324
Then I'll help your pups sleep

40:54.660 --> 40:56.704
Sleep, sleep…

40:56.787 --> 40:59.165
She left behind her three children…

41:03.711 --> 41:04.920
at the age of 29.

41:40.080 --> 41:41.749
If you cry, you'll be hungry.

41:41.832 --> 41:43.083
So eat while you cry.

41:49.006 --> 41:51.258
What should I do now?

41:52.843 --> 41:53.928
What should I do?

41:55.638 --> 41:56.764
This morning,

41:58.682 --> 41:59.600
my mom

42:00.434 --> 42:01.644
passed away.

42:03.270 --> 42:04.188
But…

42:05.814 --> 42:06.774
but…

42:12.905 --> 42:14.823
I miss her already.

42:17.284 --> 42:19.203
I miss my mom already.

42:22.164 --> 42:23.165
I…

42:23.249 --> 42:25.459
I miss her so much.

42:30.130 --> 42:31.549
Mom.

42:35.052 --> 42:36.095
Mom.

42:43.310 --> 42:46.397
Ae-sun, Sun-nam, and Sun-bong.

42:47.106 --> 42:49.900
Think about it.
You all have "sun" in your names.

42:49.984 --> 42:51.402
You are connected by blood.

42:53.362 --> 42:54.905
Look at you.

42:54.989 --> 42:56.699
A scruffy dog might ask to marry you.

42:58.075 --> 43:00.327
I have no choice.
It's yellowtail season now.

43:00.411 --> 43:03.706
I need to go on the boat
to feed your younger siblings.

43:07.543 --> 43:10.421
If you go to your uncle's,
you'll just end up being a maid.

43:11.171 --> 43:16.677
A maid who takes care of her siblings is
more fulfilled than one caring for others.

43:16.760 --> 43:17.928
I won't be a maid.

43:19.805 --> 43:21.807
Mom told me not to live like that.

43:22.725 --> 43:23.601
Hey, Ae-sun.

43:24.268 --> 43:27.271
Your mom can't rest in peace
if your siblings live like beggars.

43:29.732 --> 43:31.692
Just during yellowtail season.

43:33.277 --> 43:34.111
Okay?

43:34.820 --> 43:37.072
Are you going to just let this field rot?

43:37.156 --> 43:38.991
Why waste perfectly fine land?

43:50.711 --> 43:53.672
Just until Sun-bong
is out of diapers, okay?

44:04.391 --> 44:05.225
Let's go.

44:09.772 --> 44:12.232
Just until Sun-nam starts
elementary school, okay?

44:15.778 --> 44:16.862
Just wait and see.

44:17.613 --> 44:19.657
As the flower dye fades
from your fingernails,

44:19.740 --> 44:21.867
the living will forget and carry on.

44:27.539 --> 44:28.749
Life goes on and on.

44:29.249 --> 44:31.043
Just as fingernails grow,

44:31.794 --> 44:33.295
new days rush in.

44:33.796 --> 44:35.547
How could you not forget?

44:39.551 --> 44:43.305
Did your business go under?
How do you always have leftover fish?

45:09.707 --> 45:10.749
I'm leaving home.

45:10.833 --> 45:11.917
POEMS OF YU CHI-HWAN

45:13.711 --> 45:17.464
Just until this upcoming trip, okay?

45:18.549 --> 45:22.010
A few more deep-sea fishing trips,
and we can find a way to survive.

45:23.929 --> 45:27.808
Other kids are taking private lessons
while I'm farming and cooking.

45:27.891 --> 45:29.601
I want to get first place too.

45:29.685 --> 45:31.603
And I want to…

45:34.773 --> 45:35.983
Just forget it.

45:39.862 --> 45:41.363
What, a Korean literature major?

45:41.447 --> 45:43.615
Is that all you want?
A Korean literature major?

45:44.116 --> 45:45.993
A poet. That's right.

45:46.076 --> 45:48.412
You said you wanted to be a poet,
didn't you?

45:48.495 --> 45:50.789
That would be wonderful. A poet--

45:54.626 --> 45:59.173
Yi Sang, Kim So-wol, and Yun Dong-ju
all majored in Korean literature, right?

45:59.256 --> 46:01.300
"If you choose to leave,

46:01.383 --> 46:03.051
weary at the sight of me,

46:03.135 --> 46:05.554
tread gently as you go."

46:06.889 --> 46:08.724
I'll lay down money before you

46:09.558 --> 46:12.352
until you become
a Korean literature major.

46:12.436 --> 46:13.270
Okay?

46:17.524 --> 46:20.861
Anyway, who paid all
of your monthly school fees?

46:21.528 --> 46:22.571
Am I just some random man?

46:22.654 --> 46:26.241
I'm like a father figure
to you now, aren't I?

46:26.742 --> 46:29.703
I'm telling you, I'll make money
and send you to college.

46:32.039 --> 46:34.291
Your uncle won't send you to college.

46:34.917 --> 46:37.795
If that family wanted to take care of you,
they would've--

46:37.878 --> 46:40.631
To the mainland, okay?

46:41.632 --> 46:43.634
To the mainland.
A college on the mainland.

46:43.717 --> 46:45.344
You swear on Sun-nam and Sun-bong?

46:47.221 --> 46:48.972
I swear on Jeon Gwang-rye!

46:49.056 --> 46:52.851
If I forget everything you've done for us,
your mom will kill me.

46:54.353 --> 46:57.481
There's an active campaign to promote
a simple and practical lifestyle

46:57.564 --> 47:00.442
by encouraging the public
to wear simplified clothing.

47:00.526 --> 47:02.611
When you're at your busiest and in a rush,

47:02.694 --> 47:06.490
wearing a long traditional skirt
is simply cumbersome and uncomfortable.

47:06.990 --> 47:12.079
The purpose of this campaign
is to improve these inactive lifestyles.

47:14.248 --> 47:17.084
SPY DETECTION CAMPAIGN PERIOD

47:27.344 --> 47:29.012
ICE

47:55.664 --> 47:56.707
YANG GWAN-SIK

47:57.958 --> 47:59.126
Would you like some?

47:59.668 --> 48:00.752
No, I want cabbages.

48:01.336 --> 48:03.630
Exactly. Do you want some cabbages?

48:05.382 --> 48:06.842
Do you also sell cabbages?

48:06.925 --> 48:08.427
Well, they are sweet.

48:10.429 --> 48:11.263
Her cabbages.

48:11.847 --> 48:12.764
They are sweet.

48:16.143 --> 48:17.311
Here, check it out!

48:17.978 --> 48:19.563
Fresh, fresh catches!

48:19.646 --> 48:23.233
Freshly caught by haenyeo
just moments ago!

48:23.317 --> 48:24.902
Straight from the sea!

48:24.985 --> 48:26.153
Please stop by!

48:26.236 --> 48:29.615
Fresh sea squirt, abalone, and conch!
At an unbeatable price!

48:29.698 --> 48:31.408
Why worry about Gwang-rye's daughter?

48:31.491 --> 48:32.993
She has Steelheart by her side.

49:05.442 --> 49:07.277
They are sweet. Would you like some?

49:07.903 --> 49:08.820
Would you like some?

49:08.904 --> 49:11.740
Gwan-sik sells
all of Ae-sun's cabbages for her.

49:12.240 --> 49:15.869
The bold shortening of skirts
is promoting a decadent trend.

49:15.953 --> 49:18.080
These cabbages are sweet.
Would you like some?

49:18.163 --> 49:21.208
In Myeong-dong, Seoul,
women can be seen waltzing around

49:21.291 --> 49:23.335
with their thighs fully exposed.

49:24.753 --> 49:29.174
Now you could say
that Gwan-sik is raising Ae-sun.

49:31.468 --> 49:36.139
Now there are calls for strict measures
to combat the decadent trend.

49:36.723 --> 49:40.435
"First, they said to wear shorter clothes,
and now they're complaining!"

49:40.519 --> 49:43.397
Arguing like this will only make
our testing lives even harder.

49:43.480 --> 49:44.356
CREATION AND CRITICISM

49:44.439 --> 49:45.649
Would you like some?

49:46.608 --> 49:49.736
The cabbages are sweet,
especially the ones over there.

49:50.237 --> 49:52.030
I'm sure everything is sweet to you.

49:52.114 --> 49:56.118
Looks like you'll have to serve
both mother-in-law and daughter-in-law.

49:56.201 --> 49:57.536
Gosh, it's just my luck.

49:58.578 --> 50:00.163
How much are the cabbages?

50:00.247 --> 50:01.707
Fifty won each, 150 for three.

50:01.790 --> 50:03.333
What kind of absurd deal is that?

50:03.417 --> 50:06.086
If one is 50 won,
then three should be 150 won.

50:08.588 --> 50:09.464
OH AE-SUN

50:09.548 --> 50:10.590
That's justice.

50:11.299 --> 50:13.927
Hey, who talks about justice
when buying cabbages?

50:14.011 --> 50:16.013
Did I even ask for the price of three?

50:16.722 --> 50:19.057
I make peanuts selling cabbages,

50:19.141 --> 50:21.643
but everyone wants to haggle
over the price.

50:21.727 --> 50:23.228
I wanted to raise awareness--

50:23.311 --> 50:25.605
Who cares about awareness
when buying cabbages?

50:27.149 --> 50:28.525
-Well…
-There he goes!

50:29.109 --> 50:31.570
-Do you want some?
-He won't allow a second complaint.

50:31.653 --> 50:32.946
I gave birth to a fool.

50:33.989 --> 50:36.033
Give me one. Just one.

50:38.785 --> 50:41.038
Doesn't Ae-sun have hands or something?

50:41.121 --> 50:42.664
I didn't make him do it.

50:42.748 --> 50:44.833
He's doing it because he likes it.

50:44.916 --> 50:46.043
She's not making me.

50:48.295 --> 50:51.131
I should've raised a stray dog
instead of him.

50:51.673 --> 50:55.260
You'll wish you were dead
if you get caught hanging out together.

50:55.343 --> 50:57.679
They have the exuberance
and fearlessness of youth.

50:57.763 --> 50:59.431
As if they'd be scared of a granny.

51:03.810 --> 51:04.936
Oh no.

51:11.359 --> 51:12.861
-Out of the way!
-Grandma!

51:17.365 --> 51:20.494
Haven't I told you
not to let her open the stall next to him?

51:20.577 --> 51:22.662
Why do you keep coming all the way here?

51:22.746 --> 51:25.665
Haven't you heard
daughters inherit their mothers' fate?

51:25.749 --> 51:28.710
Her mom's spirit is still lingering
to protect her.

51:28.794 --> 51:32.047
Why would you let her stay
next to my grandson?

51:32.130 --> 51:33.507
That hag needs a baptism.

51:33.590 --> 51:35.550
Barnacles and whelks are no different!

51:36.051 --> 51:38.804
Ae-sun, that brat!

51:38.887 --> 51:39.805
You brat!

51:39.888 --> 51:42.766
I don't even want him.
Yang Gwan-sik? No, thank you!

51:43.350 --> 51:44.601
No, thank you!

51:44.684 --> 51:45.936
This is insane.

51:46.019 --> 51:47.395
-Ae-sun, that brat!
-Mother.

51:47.479 --> 51:49.481
Ae-sun, that brat!

52:03.995 --> 52:05.872
Some faced the "No, thank you days"

52:06.623 --> 52:09.042
and did not back down.

54:54.332 --> 54:59.337
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS."

55:06.636 --> 55:09.014
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
